{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"ee3a5688c1e1101db4b99036b87d20525c6a89a400c17654d3d6873ea5f5727b","digest":{"component_or_area":"Graph linking / dependency recording","key_entities":["src/rebar/graph/_links.py:207","src/rebar/graph/_links.py:213","src/rebar/graph/_links.py:269","src/rebar/graph/_links.py:282","src/rebar/_lib_writes.py:615","src/rebar/_commands/composer.py:629","src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:213-214","add_dependency","link_core","rebar.link","_python_leaf","link_tickets","quiet","_emit_redirect","contextlib.redirect_stdout"],"problem_keywords":["cross-subtree link escalation","silent failure","return value propagation","stdout suppression","MCP protocol","library caller","redirect record"],"propositions":["Escalated cross-subtree links silently record different endpoints than requested, with callers informed only of success via stdout that is not returned","The redirect record is printed to stdout only and never returned, so library and MCP callers cannot access the information that escalation occurred","The quiet context manager suppresses stdout for MCP and in-process reconciler paths, which is load-bearing for protocol integrity but causes the escalation record to be unreachable","Return values must propagate through five call layers: add_dependency, link_core, _link closure, _python_leaf, and rebar.link(), currently dropping the value at three points","The MCP link_tickets tool must report escalation as a string suffix to its ok response when the recorded endpoints differ from the requested ones"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":17878002